<title>SOUTH AFRICA: WB Holdings year share up, div surges.</title>
<headline>WB Holdings year share up, div surges.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>		 (million of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	    58	vs 23</p>
<p>    Final div  (cts)   13	making  18 vs 8</p>
<p>    Retained profit    3.8     vs 1.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		5.9     vs 2.1</p>
<p>    Tax		    0.4     vs rebate 0.04</p>
<p>    Interest paid	0.1     vs 0.01</p>
<p>    Turnover	    19.9     vs 14.1</p>
<p>Div payable May 23</p>
<p>on register April 18</p>
<p>Full name: WB Holdings Ltd (fruit producer, exporter)</p>
<p>NOTE:  The group said it was investing 4.4 million rand in new  plantings, building and equipment and would employ more permanent labour rather than migrant labour.</p>
<p>The late start to warmer weather this year had delayed picking and it was unlikely that the 1997 crop would be as large as that of last year. The weaker rand was expected to compensate for the decline in export volumes.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
